{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "F58JoinGateRetainsItsMatchSet",
    "description": "F58's CONTROL, and the half that must keep passing. F58 -- EarthSciML/EarthSciAST#418, a join-gated `faq` retaining ~80 bytes per candidate pair in a cache that never evicted -- was fixed by PR #420 (the index holds its pairs once instead of four times, and both gate caches got a resident-pair budget) and PR #423 (a gate is PRICED before it is built, and one that would materialise more pairs than the tuples it could prune is declined). Both merged 2026-09-19 and the pin moved to them.\n\nSO THIS FILE CHANGED JOBS RATHER THAN BEING DELETED. A retired finding's repro is normally deleted -- F3, F5, F13, F14, F20 and F21 all were -- and this one is kept for the reason F57's and F28's controls are kept: the thing it measures can come back, it is measured in a NUMBER rather than in a pass/fail, and nothing else in this tree would notice. `tools/check-join-gate-memory.py` now asserts the marginal cost stays BELOW 50 bytes a candidate pair, where it once asserted it stayed above. 79 before the fix, 34 after.\n\nWHAT IT IS. `total` is a textbook star-join aggregate: for each output row, sum a measure over the fact rows sharing its key, once per value of a free axis. It is the shape of `rtMode_rate` in onroad/model.esm, and of the `bin_usedFraction` clause that found F58 -- 656 source bins against the 1,424,430-row national `fuelusagefraction` table on a SIX-VALUED fuel-type key, 166,861,800 candidate pairs, while a sibling clause cut that table to single digits.\n\nIT IS SELF-CONTAINED ON PURPOSE, which is why the `1 + (i-1) mod n` idiom is written out twice rather than factored into an expression template the way CLAUDE.md asks. A template is imported by reference, and this file has to be copy-and-runnable by someone who has only the upstream issue in front of them. It is quoted verbatim in EarthSciML/EarthSciAST#418.\n\nTHE FOUR METAPARAMETERS ARE THE MEASUREMENT. Candidate pairs are n_out x (n_big / n_key); declared arrays are (2 x n_big + n_out x n_free + n_free) doubles; the answer is n_out x n_free doubles. `n_big` moves both the arrays and the pairs, `n_key` moves the pairs alone (the fanout), `n_out` moves the answer, and `n_free` moves NEITHER the pairs nor the memory -- only the work, which is the odometer streaming an ungated range as it should.\n\nAT THESE DEFAULTS, on the merged toolchain: 16 MB of declared arrays, a 0.03 MB answer, and 0.12 GB of peak resident memory where the same document cost 0.26 GB before. PLAN.md §7.3.8 has what that was worth on the model itself -- every RunSpec in this tree now evaluates under 1 GB, against 6.6 to 38.7 before.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "probe",
      "performance"
    ]
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "n_big": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 1000000,
      "description": "Rows in the fact table."
    },
    "n_key": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 1000,
      "description": "Distinct join keys. Each key carries n_big/n_key fact rows."
    },
    "n_out": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 1000,
      "description": "Rows in the output relation, one per key when n_out == n_key."
    },
    "n_free": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 4,
      "description": "Width of the axis the join does NOT gate. THIS IS THE ONE THAT MATTERS."
    }
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "big_rows": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "n_big"
    },
    "out_rows": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "n_out"
    },
    "free_rows": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "n_free"
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "JoinAggregateScaling": {
      "tolerance": {
        "rel": 1e-12
      },
      "variables": {
        "big_key": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "big_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The fact row's key: 1 + (a-1) mod n_key."
        },
        "big_value": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "big_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The measure being summed. 1.0, so the answer is a count."
        },
        "out_key": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "out_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The output row's key: 1 + (o-1) mod n_key."
        },
        "free_weight": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "free_rows"
          ],
          "description": "A per-free-axis factor. 1.0."
        },
        "total": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "out_rows",
            "free_rows"
          ],
          "description": "n_big/n_key for every cell. The OUTPUT is n_out x n_free doubles; the enumeration space is n_big x n_free."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": "big_key",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "faq",
            "args": [],
            "output_idx": [
              "a"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "a": {
                "from": "big_rows"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "+",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "-",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "-",
                      "args": [
                        "a",
                        1
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        "n_key",
                        {
                          "op": "floor",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "/",
                              "args": [
                                {
                                  "op": "-",
                                  "args": [
                                    "a",
                                    1
                                  ]
                                },
                                "n_key"
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                1
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "big_value",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "faq",
            "args": [],
            "output_idx": [
              "a"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "a": {
                "from": "big_rows"
              }
            },
            "expr": 1.0
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "out_key",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "faq",
            "args": [],
            "output_idx": [
              "o"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "o": {
                "from": "out_rows"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "+",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "-",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "-",
                      "args": [
                        "o",
                        1
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        "n_key",
                        {
                          "op": "floor",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "/",
                              "args": [
                                {
                                  "op": "-",
                                  "args": [
                                    "o",
                                    1
                                  ]
                                },
                                "n_key"
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                1
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "free_weight",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "faq",
            "args": [],
            "output_idx": [
              "f"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "f": {
                "from": "free_rows"
              }
            },
            "expr": 1.0
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "total",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "faq",
            "args": [],
            "semiring": "sum_product",
            "output_idx": [
              "o",
              "f"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "o": {
                "from": "out_rows"
              },
              "f": {
                "from": "free_rows"
              },
              "a": {
                "from": "big_rows"
              }
            },
            "join": [
              {
                "on": [
                  [
                    "out_key",
                    "big_key"
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ],
            "expr": {
              "op": "*",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": [
                    "big_value",
                    "a"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": [
                    "free_weight",
                    "f"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "every_cell_is_the_fanout",
          "description": "Each output key matches n_big/n_key fact rows and each contributes 1.0, so every cell is that fanout, on every free-axis slice.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "total",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1000.0,
              "coords": {
                "out_rows": 1,
                "free_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "total",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1000.0,
              "coords": {
                "out_rows": 1000,
                "free_rows": 4
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
